{
  "title": "Stage 3: Expired and the wrong name",
  "summary": "Diagnose NotTimeValid and host names missing from the SAN.",
  "minutes": 15,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Briefing: dates and names",
      "body": [
        "Two new scenario lines and two new diagnoses.",
        "",
        "- `expired` makes the leaf valid 2028-01-01 to 2029-01-01, so at 2030-06-01 the chain reports `NotTimeValid`. Clients say `certificate has expired`, `NET::ERR_CERT_DATE_INVALID`, or `RemoteCertificateChainErrors` with `NotTimeValid`.",
        "- **Name mismatch** is not a chain problem at all: the chain can be perfect and the name still wrong. Check the host against the **SAN only** with `MatchesHostname(host, allowWildcards: true, allowCommonName: false)`, like browsers (`NET::ERR_CERT_COMMON_NAME_INVALID`) and .NET (`RemoteCertificateNameMismatch`).",
        "",
        "The order of diagnoses is fixed: missing intermediate, untrusted root, expired, name mismatch.",
        "",
        "Input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "host api.shop.example",
        "names shop.example www.shop.example",
        "sends leaf intermediate",
        "trusts root",
        "expired",
        "```",
        "",
        "Output:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "host: api.shop.example",
        "server sends: CN=shop.example, CN=Doctor Issuing CA",
        "client trusts: CN=Doctor Root",
        "chain: NotTimeValid",
        "PROBLEM expired: CN=shop.example expired on 2029-01-01",
        "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates",
        "  fix: renew the certificate and deploy the new one",
        "PROBLEM name mismatch: api.shop.example is not in the certificate (SAN: shop.example, www.shop.example)",
        "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -ext subjectAltName",
        "  fix: reissue with -addext \"subjectAltName=DNS:api.shop.example\"",
        "verdict: 2 problems",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Match each client error to its diagnosis.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "`NET::ERR_CERT_COMMON_NAME_INVALID`",
          "name mismatch"
        ],
        [
          "`certificate has expired` (openssl error 10)",
          "expired"
        ],
        [
          "`unable to get local issuer certificate` (error 20)",
          "missing intermediate"
        ],
        [
          "`self-signed certificate in certificate chain` (error 19)",
          "untrusted root"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "A certificate has `CN=shop.example` and SAN `DNS:www.shop.example`. The client connects to `shop.example`. Modern browsers say?",
      "options": [
        "Name mismatch: when a SAN is present, the CN is ignored",
        "Fine, the CN matches",
        "Fine, `www.` is optional",
        "Expired"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "RFC 6125 and the CA/Browser Forum rules: browsers check the SAN only. That's why chain-doctor turns the CN fallback off."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does `openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates` print for chain-doctor's expired leaf? Type the `notAfter=` line.",
      "code": [
        "openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates"
      ],
      "answer": "notAfter=Jan  1 00:00:00 2029 GMT",
      "verify": false,
      "explain": "openssl prints dates as `MMM dd HH:MM:SS YYYY GMT`, with the day padded by a space. The first line would be `notBefore=Jan  1 00:00:00 2028 GMT`.",
      "accept": [
        "notAfter=Jan 1 00:00:00 2029 GMT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "write",
      "title": "chain-doctor: expired and name mismatch",
      "prompt": [
        "Add the `expired` scenario line (the leaf becomes valid 2028-01-01 to 2029-01-01) and two diagnoses, after the untrusted-root one:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "PROBLEM expired: CN=LEAF expired on YYYY-MM-DD",
        "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates",
        "  fix: renew the certificate and deploy the new one",
        "```",
        "",
        "```text",
        "PROBLEM name mismatch: HOST is not in the certificate (SAN: NAME, NAME)",
        "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -ext subjectAltName",
        "  fix: reissue with -addext \"subjectAltName=DNS:HOST\"",
        "```",
        "",
        "Expired comes from the chain's `NotTimeValid`; the date is the leaf's `NotAfter` in UTC. Name mismatch comes from `MatchesHostname` with the CN fallback off.",
        "",
        "Input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "host api.shop.example",
        "names shop.example www.shop.example",
        "sends leaf intermediate",
        "trusts root",
        "expired",
        "```",
        "",
        "Output:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "host: api.shop.example",
        "server sends: CN=shop.example, CN=Doctor Issuing CA",
        "client trusts: CN=Doctor Root",
        "chain: NotTimeValid",
        "PROBLEM expired: CN=shop.example expired on 2029-01-01",
        "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates",
        "  fix: renew the certificate and deploy the new one",
        "PROBLEM name mismatch: api.shop.example is not in the certificate (SAN: shop.example, www.shop.example)",
        "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -ext subjectAltName",
        "  fix: reissue with -addext \"subjectAltName=DNS:api.shop.example\"",
        "verdict: 2 problems",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;",
        "",
        "var at = new DateTime(2030, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc);",
        "var root = MakeCa(\"CN=Doctor Root\", null);",
        "var inter = MakeCa(\"CN=Doctor Issuing CA\", root);",
        "",
        "var input = new List<string>();",
        "string? text;",
        "while ((text = Console.ReadLine()) != null) input.Add(text);",
        "Diagnose(input);",
        "",
        "int Diagnose(List<string> scenario)",
        "{",
        "    string host = \"\";",
        "    string[]? names = null;",
        "    var sends = new List<string>();",
        "    bool trusts = false;",
        "    bool expired = false;",
        "    string eku = \"serverAuth\";",
        "    foreach (var raw in scenario)",
        "    {",
        "        string line = raw.Trim();",
        "        if (line == \"\" || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "        var words = line.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);",
        "        switch (words[0])",
        "        {",
        "            case \"host\": host = words.Length > 1 ? words[1] : \"\"; break;",
        "            case \"names\": names = words[1..]; break;",
        "            case \"sends\": sends = words[1..].ToList(); break;",
        "            case \"trusts\": trusts = words.Length > 1 && words[1] == \"root\"; break;",
        "            default: Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown line '{line}'\"); break;",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "    if (host == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: no host line\"); return -1; }",
        "    if (!sends.Contains(\"leaf\")) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: the server must send a leaf\"); return -1; }",
        "    var bad = sends.FirstOrDefault(s => s != \"leaf\" && s != \"intermediate\" && s != \"root\");",
        "    if (bad != null) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown certificate '{bad}'\"); return -1; }",
        "    if (names == null || names.Length == 0) names = new[] { host };",
        "",
        "    var leaf = MakeLeaf(names, expired, eku);",
        "    var byName = new Dictionary<string, X509Certificate2> { [\"leaf\"] = leaf, [\"intermediate\"] = inter, [\"root\"] = root };",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"host: {host}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"server sends: {string.Join(\", \", sends.Select(s => byName[s].Subject))}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"client trusts: {(trusts ? root.Subject : \"nothing\")}\");",
        "",
        "    using var chain = new X509Chain();",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.TrustMode = X509ChainTrustMode.CustomRootTrust;",
        "    if (trusts) chain.ChainPolicy.CustomTrustStore.Add(root);",
        "    foreach (var s in sends.Where(s => s != \"leaf\").Distinct()) chain.ChainPolicy.ExtraStore.Add(byName[s]);",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.ApplicationPolicy.Add(new Oid(\"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\"));",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.RevocationMode = X509RevocationMode.NoCheck;",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.DisableCertificateDownloads = true;",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.VerificationTime = at;",
        "    chain.Build(leaf);",
        "    var flags = chain.ChainStatus.Select(s => s.Status).Where(f => f != X509ChainStatusFlags.NoError)",
        "        .Distinct().OrderBy(f => f.ToString(), StringComparer.Ordinal).ToList();",
        "    Console.WriteLine(flags.Count == 0 ? \"chain: valid\" : $\"chain: {string.Join(\", \", flags)}\");",
        "",
        "   int problems = 0;",
        "   bool partial = flags.Contains(X509ChainStatusFlags.PartialChain);",
        "   if (partial && !sends.Contains(\"intermediate\"))",
        "   {",
        "       problems++;",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"PROBLEM missing intermediate: the server does not send {inter.Subject}\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"  confirm: openssl s_client -connect {host}:443 -servername {host} -showcerts\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  fix: cat leaf.pem intermediate.pem > fullchain.pem, then serve fullchain.pem\");",
        "   }",
        "   if (flags.Contains(X509ChainStatusFlags.UntrustedRoot) || (partial && sends.Contains(\"intermediate\")))",
        "   {",
        "       problems++;",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"PROBLEM untrusted root: the client does not trust {root.Subject}\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  confirm: openssl verify -CAfile root.pem -untrusted intermediate.pem leaf.pem\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  fix (Linux): sudo cp root.pem /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/root.crt && sudo update-ca-certificates\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(@\"  fix (Windows): Import-Certificate -FilePath root.cer -CertStoreLocation Cert:\\LocalMachine\\Root\");",
        "   }",
        "   Console.WriteLine(problems == 0 ? \"verdict: healthy\" : $\"verdict: {problems} problem{(problems == 1 ? \"\" : \"s\")}\");",
        "   return problems;",
        "}",
        "",
        "X509Certificate2 MakeCa(string subject, X509Certificate2? issuer)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(subject, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, issuer != null, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    if (issuer == null) return req.CreateSelfSigned(Day(2020), Day(2050));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(issuer, true, false));",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(issuer, Day(2020), Day(2050), new byte[] { 0x10, 0x01 });",
        "    return pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key);",
        "}",
        "",
        "X509Certificate2 MakeLeaf(string[] dns, bool isExpired, string usage)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + dns[0], key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(false, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.DigitalSignature, true));",
        "    string oid = usage switch { \"clientAuth\" => \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.2\", \"codeSigning\" => \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.3\", _ => \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\" };",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509EnhancedKeyUsageExtension(new OidCollection { new Oid(oid) }, false));",
        "    var san = new SubjectAlternativeNameBuilder();",
        "    foreach (var d in dns) san.AddDnsName(d);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(san.Build());",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(inter, true, false));",
        "    return req.Create(inter, Day(isExpired ? 2028 : 2030), Day(isExpired ? 2029 : 2031), new byte[] { 0x20, 0x01 });",
        "}",
        "",
        "static DateTimeOffset Day(int year) => new DateTimeOffset(year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;",
        "",
        "var at = new DateTime(2030, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc);",
        "var root = MakeCa(\"CN=Doctor Root\", null);",
        "var inter = MakeCa(\"CN=Doctor Issuing CA\", root);",
        "",
        "var input = new List<string>();",
        "string? text;",
        "while ((text = Console.ReadLine()) != null) input.Add(text);",
        "Diagnose(input);",
        "",
        "int Diagnose(List<string> scenario)",
        "{",
        "    string host = \"\";",
        "    string[]? names = null;",
        "    var sends = new List<string>();",
        "    bool trusts = false;",
        "    bool expired = false;",
        "    string eku = \"serverAuth\";",
        "    foreach (var raw in scenario)",
        "    {",
        "        string line = raw.Trim();",
        "        if (line == \"\" || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "        var words = line.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);",
        "        switch (words[0])",
        "        {",
        "            case \"host\": host = words.Length > 1 ? words[1] : \"\"; break;",
        "            case \"names\": names = words[1..]; break;",
        "            case \"sends\": sends = words[1..].ToList(); break;",
        "            case \"trusts\": trusts = words.Length > 1 && words[1] == \"root\"; break;",
        "           case \"expired\": expired = true; break;",
        "            default: Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown line '{line}'\"); break;",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "    if (host == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: no host line\"); return -1; }",
        "    if (!sends.Contains(\"leaf\")) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: the server must send a leaf\"); return -1; }",
        "    var bad = sends.FirstOrDefault(s => s != \"leaf\" && s != \"intermediate\" && s != \"root\");",
        "    if (bad != null) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown certificate '{bad}'\"); return -1; }",
        "    if (names == null || names.Length == 0) names = new[] { host };",
        "",
        "    var leaf = MakeLeaf(names, expired, eku);",
        "    var byName = new Dictionary<string, X509Certificate2> { [\"leaf\"] = leaf, [\"intermediate\"] = inter, [\"root\"] = root };",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"host: {host}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"server sends: {string.Join(\", \", sends.Select(s => byName[s].Subject))}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"client trusts: {(trusts ? root.Subject : \"nothing\")}\");",
        "",
        "    using var chain = new X509Chain();",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.TrustMode = X509ChainTrustMode.CustomRootTrust;",
        "    if (trusts) chain.ChainPolicy.CustomTrustStore.Add(root);",
        "    foreach (var s in sends.Where(s => s != \"leaf\").Distinct()) chain.ChainPolicy.ExtraStore.Add(byName[s]);",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.ApplicationPolicy.Add(new Oid(\"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\"));",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.RevocationMode = X509RevocationMode.NoCheck;",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.DisableCertificateDownloads = true;",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.VerificationTime = at;",
        "    chain.Build(leaf);",
        "    var flags = chain.ChainStatus.Select(s => s.Status).Where(f => f != X509ChainStatusFlags.NoError)",
        "        .Distinct().OrderBy(f => f.ToString(), StringComparer.Ordinal).ToList();",
        "    Console.WriteLine(flags.Count == 0 ? \"chain: valid\" : $\"chain: {string.Join(\", \", flags)}\");",
        "",
        "   int problems = 0;",
        "   bool partial = flags.Contains(X509ChainStatusFlags.PartialChain);",
        "   if (partial && !sends.Contains(\"intermediate\"))",
        "   {",
        "       problems++;",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"PROBLEM missing intermediate: the server does not send {inter.Subject}\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"  confirm: openssl s_client -connect {host}:443 -servername {host} -showcerts\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  fix: cat leaf.pem intermediate.pem > fullchain.pem, then serve fullchain.pem\");",
        "   }",
        "   if (flags.Contains(X509ChainStatusFlags.UntrustedRoot) || (partial && sends.Contains(\"intermediate\")))",
        "   {",
        "       problems++;",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"PROBLEM untrusted root: the client does not trust {root.Subject}\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  confirm: openssl verify -CAfile root.pem -untrusted intermediate.pem leaf.pem\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  fix (Linux): sudo cp root.pem /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/root.crt && sudo update-ca-certificates\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(@\"  fix (Windows): Import-Certificate -FilePath root.cer -CertStoreLocation Cert:\\LocalMachine\\Root\");",
        "   }",
        "   if (flags.Contains(X509ChainStatusFlags.NotTimeValid))",
        "   {",
        "       problems++;",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"PROBLEM expired: {leaf.Subject} expired on {leaf.NotAfter.ToUniversalTime():yyyy-MM-dd}\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  fix: renew the certificate and deploy the new one\");",
        "   }",
        "   if (!leaf.MatchesHostname(host, allowWildcards: true, allowCommonName: false))",
        "   {",
        "       problems++;",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"PROBLEM name mismatch: {host} is not in the certificate (SAN: {string.Join(\", \", names)})\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine(\"  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -ext subjectAltName\");",
        "       Console.WriteLine($\"  fix: reissue with -addext \\\"subjectAltName=DNS:{host}\\\"\");",
        "   }",
        "   Console.WriteLine(problems == 0 ? \"verdict: healthy\" : $\"verdict: {problems} problem{(problems == 1 ? \"\" : \"s\")}\");",
        "   return problems;",
        "}",
        "",
        "X509Certificate2 MakeCa(string subject, X509Certificate2? issuer)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(subject, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, issuer != null, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    if (issuer == null) return req.CreateSelfSigned(Day(2020), Day(2050));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(issuer, true, false));",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(issuer, Day(2020), Day(2050), new byte[] { 0x10, 0x01 });",
        "    return pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key);",
        "}",
        "",
        "X509Certificate2 MakeLeaf(string[] dns, bool isExpired, string usage)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + dns[0], key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(false, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.DigitalSignature, true));",
        "    string oid = usage switch { \"clientAuth\" => \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.2\", \"codeSigning\" => \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.3\", _ => \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\" };",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509EnhancedKeyUsageExtension(new OidCollection { new Oid(oid) }, false));",
        "    var san = new SubjectAlternativeNameBuilder();",
        "    foreach (var d in dns) san.AddDnsName(d);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(san.Build());",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(inter, true, false));",
        "    return req.Create(inter, Day(isExpired ? 2028 : 2030), Day(isExpired ? 2029 : 2031), new byte[] { 0x20, 0x01 });",
        "}",
        "",
        "static DateTimeOffset Day(int year) => new DateTimeOffset(year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Add `case \"expired\": expired = true; break;` and pass `expired` to `MakeLeaf`.",
        "`leaf.NotAfter.ToUniversalTime():yyyy-MM-dd` inside the interpolated string.",
        "`if (!leaf.MatchesHostname(host, allowWildcards: true, allowCommonName: false))`"
      ],
      "carry": true,
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "expired leaf",
          "stdin": [
            "host shop.example",
            "sends leaf intermediate",
            "trusts root",
            "expired"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "host: shop.example",
            "server sends: CN=shop.example, CN=Doctor Issuing CA",
            "client trusts: CN=Doctor Root",
            "chain: NotTimeValid",
            "PROBLEM expired: CN=shop.example expired on 2029-01-01",
            "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates",
            "  fix: renew the certificate and deploy the new one",
            "verdict: 1 problem"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "name mismatch",
          "stdin": [
            "host api.shop.example",
            "names shop.example www.shop.example",
            "sends leaf intermediate",
            "trusts root"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "host: api.shop.example",
            "server sends: CN=shop.example, CN=Doctor Issuing CA",
            "client trusts: CN=Doctor Root",
            "chain: valid",
            "PROBLEM name mismatch: api.shop.example is not in the certificate (SAN: shop.example, www.shop.example)",
            "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -ext subjectAltName",
            "  fix: reissue with -addext \"subjectAltName=DNS:api.shop.example\"",
            "verdict: 1 problem"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "expired and wrong name together",
          "stdin": [
            "host api.shop.example",
            "names shop.example www.shop.example",
            "sends leaf intermediate",
            "trusts root",
            "expired"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "host: api.shop.example",
            "server sends: CN=shop.example, CN=Doctor Issuing CA",
            "client trusts: CN=Doctor Root",
            "chain: NotTimeValid",
            "PROBLEM expired: CN=shop.example expired on 2029-01-01",
            "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -dates",
            "  fix: renew the certificate and deploy the new one",
            "PROBLEM name mismatch: api.shop.example is not in the certificate (SAN: shop.example, www.shop.example)",
            "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -ext subjectAltName",
            "  fix: reissue with -addext \"subjectAltName=DNS:api.shop.example\"",
            "verdict: 2 problems"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a CN that is not in the SAN does not count",
          "stdin": [
            "host shop.example",
            "names www.shop.example",
            "sends leaf intermediate",
            "trusts root"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "host: shop.example",
            "server sends: CN=www.shop.example, CN=Doctor Issuing CA",
            "client trusts: CN=Doctor Root",
            "chain: valid",
            "PROBLEM name mismatch: shop.example is not in the certificate (SAN: www.shop.example)",
            "  confirm: openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -ext subjectAltName",
            "  fix: reissue with -addext \"subjectAltName=DNS:shop.example\"",
            "verdict: 1 problem"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "missing intermediate still found",
          "stdin": [
            "host shop.example",
            "sends leaf",
            "trusts root"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "host: shop.example",
            "server sends: CN=shop.example",
            "client trusts: CN=Doctor Root",
